00:06:16.380 --> 00:06:20.419
Speaking of which, several people asked why
this was oval and not a circle.

00:06:20.420 --> 00:06:22.960
It’s a map projection of the distant universe.

00:06:22.960 --> 00:06:27.140
The entire inside of the cosmic horizon sphere,
flattened into a plane.

00:06:27.150 --> 00:06:30.240
It’s oval for the same reason this map of
the Earth is oval.

00:06:30.240 --> 00:06:34.050
Bobby Harper asked what aliens would see if
they lived on the edge of the universe?

00:06:34.050 --> 00:06:35.229
No edge!

00:06:35.229 --> 00:06:38.440
The universe is either infinite or it curves
back on itself.

00:06:38.440 --> 00:06:40.040
Those are your only options.

00:06:40.040 --> 00:06:41.480
The universe doesn’t have any edges.

00:06:41.480 --> 00:06:43.920
But, if you mean the edge of our observable
universe,

00:06:43.920 --> 00:06:46.940
they would just see their own observable universe
around themselves.

00:06:46.940 --> 00:06:50.180
Technically, everyone has their own observable
universe around them.

00:06:50.180 --> 00:06:52.960
We’re just all a little too close together to notice
a difference.

00:06:52.960 --> 00:06:56.960
